# Testing Standards

## Tooling

- pytest + pytest-asyncio + pytest-cov
- Run: `make test` (full suite) or `make test-billing` (single module)
- CI uses ephemeral Postgres 16 + Redis 7.2 — set `DATABASE_URL` and `REDIS_URL`

## Test Structure (current)

```
tests/
├── conftest.py              # Shared fixtures (async session, redis, settings)
├── unit/                    # Engine, billing, ingestion, dashboard helpers
└── fixtures/                # Planned: golden/ + providers/ (not required yet)
```

Current unit coverage includes billing gates, Geotab status map, duty filter, PC rest, 34h restart/weekly, day builder, alert detail/filters, and backtest replay.

## Patterns

```python
@pytest.mark.asyncio
async def test_starter_tier_blocks_voice_ivr():
    gate = require_tier_capability(lambda caps: caps.allow_voice_ivr)
    with pytest.raises(HTTPException) as exc_info:
        await gate(tenant)
    assert exc_info.value.status_code == 402
```

- Mark async tests with `@pytest.mark.asyncio`
- Import directly from `app.*` — no test-only wrappers
- Engine changes require edge-case unit tests per `CONTRIBUTING.md`
- When golden fixtures are added, golden diffs block merge; coverage % remains secondary to correctness
